{
  "$comment": "Whether a quota window's current burn rate lasts to its reset, derived from the reading alone. `used_percent`, `resets_at`, and `duration_seconds` are the whole input; `now` is the reader's clock. Every runtime answers this file: `packages/quota-model` (`quotaPace`), `packages/service` (`pace`), and `packages/apple-shared` (`QuotaPace`). `expected_headline` is the glance-surface sentence (`Expected to last until reset` / `May run out about 2h before reset`); `expected_detail` is the detail-surface tempo explanation (`Using quota faster than an even pace (+70 points)` / slower / at an even pace). Both are answered by `apps/web/src/lib/format.ts` and `QuotaPaceCopy`; they are null where there is no pace. See ADR 0035.",
